>>
Rule 1 (each input matrix must be 2-D to avoid the 1-D error)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 2
>>
Rule 2 (3-matrix chain: all are 2-D and inner dimensions align)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_3) = 2 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_2, 0) ∧ shape(v_2, 1) = shape(v_3, 0)
>>
Rule 3 (matrices container must hold at least two tensors)
{v_1 : list(tensor) ⊎ tuple(tensor)} |= v_1.len ≥ 2
